  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The game unraveled in the middle innings. Arizona scored five in the fifth after the Yankees led by three, and a deficit they clawed back to once never returned.",
    "what_this_means": "They had chances to finish it. Lombard went deep for two runs and kept them in a game that never settled. Warren's exit after 4.1 innings meant the bullpen had to hold a lead they couldn't extend. Headrick gave up two in a third of an inning. The rest of the relief corps. Hill, Schreiber, Gil. Kept it from getting worse, but the damage was already done. Eight hits. Eight strikeouts. Runners on in the first, runners on in the sixth, and nothing to show for either. This is the inconsistency that's been the thread all season. Moments of production followed by stretches of nothing, chances that don't convert into runs when it matters. The division gap grew because they couldn't hold what they built in the third inning.",
    "what_to_watch": "TB sends Nick Martinez tomorrow at 1:05 PM ET. The right-hander is running a 2.94 ERA and has given the Yankees trouble before. Rod\u00f3n has been sharp recently, carrying a 2.54 ERA over his last four starts, and that form will need to hold if the team wants to climb back.",
